<title>JAPAN: Nissan's Thai unit lays off 200 workers.</title>
<headline>Nissan's Thai unit lays off 200 workers.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nissan Motor Co Ltd said on Tuesday its Thai joint venture Siam Nissan Automobile Co had laid off 200 workers due to poor automobile demand in Thailand.</p>
<p>Siam Nissan, owned 75 percent by Siam Motor and 25 percent by Nissan, laid off 200 mainly temporary workers out of a total staff of 3,500, a Nissan spokeswoman said.</p>
</text>
